This is the most nuanced finding. The fields `difficulty`, `nonce`, and `ommers_hash` are **structurally absent** from the Engine API payload format that Prysm receives. The Ethereum Engine API (EIP-3675) deliberately excludes PoW-era header fields from the CL payload representation. Prysm's validation functions (`ValidatePayload` at `/home/gohan/runners/security-agent-1/_work/security-agent/security-agent/target_workspace/beacon-chain/core/blocks/payload.go:156`, `ValidatePayloadWhenMergeCompletes` at line 129, and `validateMergeTransitionBlock` at `/home/gohan/runners/security-agent-1/_work/security-agent/security-agent/target_workspace/beacon-chain/blockchain/process_block.go:549`) validate only the fields the CL has access to (randao, timestamp, parent_hash, merge transition). The EL is solely responsible for zeroing PoW fields in its own block header. Not bug-bounty eligible against Prysm.

